target:    uninstall.php
gate:      composer test:uninstall-data-safety
kind:      restore-defect
expect:    is gone from a SECOND blog's settings
rationale: The same defect as -01, on the MULTISITE branch. It is a separate mutation because for one review round it SURVIVED: the harness stubbed is_multisite() to false, so no behavioural case reached that branch at all, and the source-level guard written to cover it counted call sites -- which this edit leaves at the same number. Measured at the time: the suite reported 63 assertions passed with the defect in the tree. Two things had to change before this could be registered. The harness now runs every credential case a second time with is_multisite() true, and its option store is keyed on the current blog and walks a blog OTHER than the current one -- because the strip at the top of uninstall.php already covers whichever blog is standing, so a loop over the current blog alone makes the per-blog call redundant and a defect in it invisible. A gate that cannot reach a branch is not a gate for that branch, however carefully its assertions are worded.
---
--- a/uninstall.php
+++ b/uninstall.php
@@ -58,12 +58,12 @@
 
     foreach ($blogids as $blog_id) {
         switch_to_blog($blog_id);
         slimstat_uninstall_cron();
         slimstat_uninstall_transients();
-        slimstat_uninstall_credentials();
         if ($slimstat_delete_data) {
+            slimstat_uninstall_credentials();
             slimstat_uninstall($slimstat_wpdb);
         }
         restore_current_blog();
     }
 } else {
